### `or=(...)`: the union of two terms, and it has to be wider than either term alone
# @name OrGroup
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?or=(status.eq.completed,status.eq.cancelled)&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `and=(...)`: the intersection, and it has to be narrower than either term alone
# @name AndGroup
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?and=(status.eq.in_progress,is_emergency.is.true)&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The two terms of the `and` above, alone — so "narrower than either" is measured, not assumed
# @name AndLeftTermAlone
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?status=eq.in_progress&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `not.` negates the term it prefixes
# @name NotPrefix
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?not.status=eq.scheduled&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A group combined with a top-level term: the conjunction of the two
# @name GroupAndTerm
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?or=(priority.eq.1,priority.eq.4)&status=eq.scheduled&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `order=field.desc.nullslast` over the required paging key
# @name OrderDesc
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=priority.desc.nullslast,reference.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The same keys the other way round, so "the order is the one requested" is a real claim
# @name OrderAsc
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=priority.asc.nullslast,reference.desc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `select` narrows the row to the named fields, in the order they were named
# @name SelectProjection
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?select=reference,priority&order=reference.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A paged read sorted by a NULLABLE field is refused: a keyset cursor cannot place its nulls
# @name UnpageableSortKey
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=scheduled_for.desc.nullslast&limit=3
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### An unrecognised sort modifier is refused rather than ignored — an ignored one is a silent re-sort
# @name MalformedOrder
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=priority.sideways
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
